track of where it is going so updates can be provided).

TeleFun_BBS is being released as shareware with a $50 (US or Canadian,
whichever is easiest for you) registration fee. Any updates are free and
may be obtained from The Black Box BBS at (613) 394-0651.

Getting Started
---------------
To be able to use TeleFun_UserEdit you must first have created the USER.DATA
file with TeleFun_Setup.

Step 1: Run the TeleFun_UserEdit program. The program will go off to the
        appropriate directories and get some information about your BBS. You
        will be presented with a screen showing you the number of users you
        are configured for, the number of message bases, the number of
        libraries, and the number of bulletins.

Step 2: Enter the number of the user you wish to edit.

Step 3: The user's account will be presented for you. Choose the item you
        wish to edit by selecting the letter associated with that item.

Items:
-----
Account status - blank, new, valid, or Sysop
Real name - real name of user
Board name - name user wants to be known by on the BBS
Address - address of user
City - user's city
Province/State - user's province or state
Postal/Zip code - user's postal or zip code
Phone number - user's phone number (format = 123-456-7890)
Birthday - user's birthday (format = MM/DD/YYYY)
Password - user's password
Last call date - user's last date they called (format = MM/DD/YYYY HH:MM:SS)
Msg. new date - for checking for new messages (format = MM/DD/YYYY HH:MM:SS)
Lib. new date - for checking for new files (format = MM/DD/YYYY HH:MM:SS)
Account reset time - user's reset time (format = MM/DD/YYYY HH:MM:SS)
Membership expire - date user's membership expires (format = YYYYMMDD)
# times online - number of calls user has made
Public mail posted - number of public messages user has written
Private mail posted - number of private messages user has written
# files uploaded - uploaded files count
# files dloaded - download files count
# daily dloads - number of downloads already done for that day
Daily time limit - time limit user has for each 24 hour period (HH:MM)
Daily time used - time used for current 24 hour period (HH:MM)
Protocol - file transfer protocol used by that user
Score - user's score
Kbytes uploaded - number of kilobytes of files uploaded
Kbytes dloaded - number of kilobytes of files downloaded
Msg read access - message base read access status
Msg write access - message base write access status
Msg delete access - message delete access if message is not to that user
Msg edit access - message editor access if message is not to that user
Upload access - library upload access status
Dload access - library download access status
Lib file delete access - file delete access status
lib file edit access - file editor access status
Bulletin read access - bulletin read access status
Daily # guess - number of guess made at number in game Jackpot
Bits set - AmigaDOS - user access to CLI
         - game access - user access to the Fun'n Games
         - account editor access - user access to online user accounts editor
         - file editor access - access to text file editor
         - quick menu active - flag for expert menus
         - ANSI user - flag for ANSI ability of user
         - colors user - flag for color ability of user


Extra Options:
-------------
When you are asked for the user number you wish to edit, you will also see
some other options.

G - Global Modifier => this option allows you to add or delete access to
                       any of the message bases, libraries, or bulletins
                       of all user accounts without the need of going
                       through each account individually. For example, say
                       you had 10 bulletins and then you add another one
                       at a later date and you want everyone to have access
                       to it. Select G and then select 3 (for Bulletins) and
                       then select 1 for add. You will then be asked for
                       which bulletin. Enter the bulletin number and sit
                       back. TeleFun_UserEdit will go through ALL valid
                       accounts and set the access to that bulletin to ON
                       for you. You can also take away access.

P - Print => this option allows you to get a printout of any account (or
             accounts) for hard copy reference.

S - Search by name => look for a user by their name. You can enter any part
                      of their real name or board name. The program will
                      ask for verification when it finds a match. If it is
                      not the user you are looking for then select N and
                      the program will look for the next match.

Q - Quit => exit TeleFun_UserEdit

The rest is fairly straight-forward. I won't bore anyone with long detailed
explanations. Just respond to the prompts and you should be ok.
TeleFun_UserEdit has been written to aid in doing things with the user's
account without tying up the operation of the BBS.

*** NOTE ***
Values entered into a user's account will have no effect if that user is
currently online. This will be changed at a later date so that anything you
edit will happen to that user's account when you save it.
